        "original_id": "1d54ef6e-2420-50c6-b0fd-a6f403d89410",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Sparaxis, Campanula, Dierama pendulum, Hawaiian lobelioids\n- Plant Families: Iridaceae, Campanulaceae\n- Places: Cape Province, South Africa, Hawaiian Islands\n\nFacts:\n- Sparaxis, also called harlequin flower, is a genus in the family Iridaceae with about 13 species endemic to Cape Province in South Africa.\n- Campanula is one of several genera in the family Campanulaceae that share the common name bellflower.\n- Dierama pendulum was previously placed in various genera, including Ixia, Sparaxis, and Watsonia.\n- The Hawaiian lobelioids are a group of flowering plants in the bellflower family, Campanulaceae, and all are endemic to the Hawaiian Islands.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
